---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageLead from "../components/PageLead.astro";
import ArrowIcon from "../components/ArrowIcon.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About the AnalyseSpider Web Diagnostics Lab"
  description="Purpose, ownership, editorial standard, product boundary, and operating model for the new AnalyseSpider implementation."
  canonicalPath="/about"
>
  <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">About</span></nav>
  <PageLead
    title="A new web diagnostics lab, built in public"
    intro="AnalyseSpider is a 2026 implementation for people who need to inspect web evidence without turning a partial signal into a confident verdict."
    index="70"
  />
  <div class="article-shell">
    <article class="article-prose">
      <div class="takeaway"><span>Identity</span><p>{site.ownershipDisclosure}</p></div>
      <section>
        <span class="section-index">01</span>
        <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
        <p>Technical SEO and web operations produce fragments: a server-log row, a response capture, a redirect, an IP address, or a crawler string. AnalyseSpider helps organise those fragments into observed facts, bounded inferences, and explicit unknowns.</p>
        <p>The site continues the domain's broad historical technical-utility topic. The current tools, interface, writing, methods, and code are newly created.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <span class="section-index">02</span>
        <h2>What did not transfer</h2>
        <p>Former software, binaries, source code, documentation, branding, screenshots, users, customers, subscribers, authorship, and operator identity did not transfer with the domain. AnalyseSpider does not offer an old download under a new label.</p>
        <p>The <a href="/legacy">legacy map</a> records a current decision for important historical URLs: restore a legitimate user job with new work, redirect only to an equivalent successor, or retire the path.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <span class="section-index">03</span>
        <h2>Editorial standard</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Answer the diagnostic question before expanding its context.</li>
          <li>Use current primary technical documentation for changing or disputed claims.</li>
          <li>Label original observations, supported inference, and missing evidence separately.</li>
          <li>Show publication and review dates on guides, references, and lab notes.</li>
          <li>Correct factual errors without preserving a misleading earlier claim.</li>
          <li>Do not invent customers, benchmarks, field results, endorsements, or independence.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section>
        <span class="section-index">04</span>
        <h2>Product and privacy boundary</h2>
        <p>The current tools parse pasted or selected data in the browser. They do not provide unrestricted server-side fetching, active security testing, port scanning, or general crawling. No current tool uploads the submitted sample to AnalyseSpider.</p>
        <p>Local processing narrows the transfer boundary; it does not remove the user's responsibility to minimise confidential or personal data before analysis.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <span class="section-index">05</span>
        <h2>Ownership and Contextter</h2>
        <p>{site.operatorDisclosure} AnalyseSpider must remain useful without visiting or buying another product. A future Contextter workflow may be linked only after a complete standalone result and with the common ownership visible.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
    <aside class="article-aside">
      <div><span class="aside-label">Current state</span><p>Pre-launch. All canonical pages remain noindex, nofollow, and noarchive.</p></div>
      <div><span class="aside-label">Repository</span><p><a href={site.githubUrl}>Read the public source <ArrowIcon external /></a></p></div>
      <div><span class="aside-label">Corrections</span><p><a href="/contact">Report an error, privacy concern, or legacy issue <ArrowIcon /></a></p></div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
